1. Understand the problem: James delivers messages to Ms. Thompson, and then delivers 1/3 as many messages to Mr. Yu as he delivers to Ms. Thompson. We need to find the total number of messages delivered. 2. Find the number of messages to Mr. Yu: James delivers 1/3 as many messages to Mr. Yu as he delivers to Ms. Thompson. Ms. Thompson receives 66 messages, so Mr. Yu receives (1/3) * 66 messages. (1/3) * 66 = 22. 3. Find the total number of messages: James delivers 66 messages to Ms. Thompson and 22 messages to Mr. Yu. The total number of messages is 66 + 22. 66 + 22 = 88.
The total number of messages James delivers is 88.

\boxed{88}
